From 7607261bc6e46542f9550f4d7bc97c8d9e49ad06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:49:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: gas interceptor buttons v2 + hold-offset refit
 (route 00000128)

- pause/resume (CruiseSwState 4): panda grant no longer conditioned on controls_allowed (route 128 @139.2 s: a
  stale SET grant made panda judge the press a disengage while openpilot judged it a resume); brake/MAIN checked at
  press start, throughout, and at the debounced release; gas no longer blocks (engages into override, like SET).
  Python tracker mirrors it; lockstep fuzz asserts every openpilot engage has a panda grant on the same sample.
- no low-speed pedal cut: pause/resume may engage from a standstill (green-light resume); launch ceiling
  LOW_SPEED_MAX_GAS 0.12 @0 / 0.20 @5 / 0.30 @11.2 m/s (pedal is 4-5x stronger per unit below 6 m/s).
- hold-speed offset table refit on routes 127+128 at vEgo*1.0125: [0,.10,.24,.34,.43,.49,.56] @ [0..35 m/s];
  the old v^2 table was +0.10..+0.27 too high above 23 m/s (steady overspeed + 1.0 s truck gap with the P-only loop).
  On-ramp speeds (12-20 m/s) unchanged or higher.
